{"name":"Nordmann Fir","hex":"#2e7073","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fir","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Firan."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A conifer of the genus Abies.","Any pinaceous conifer of related genera, especially a Douglas fir (Pseudotsuga) or a Scots pine (Pinus sylvestris)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fir"}],"entries":[{"title":"Abies nordmanniana","blocks":[{"text":"Abies nordmanniana, the Nordmann fir or Caucasian fir, is a fir indigenous to the mountains south and east of the Black Sea, in Turkey, Georgia and the Russian Caucasus. It occurs at elevations of 900–2,200 m on mountains with precipitation of over 1,000 mm."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/%C3%96r%C3%BCmcek_Orman%C4%B1_G%C3%B6knar%C4%B1_2_Tabiat_An%C4%B1t%C4%B1.jpg/330px-%C3%96r%C3%BCmcek_Orman%C4%B1_G%C3%B6knar%C4%B1_2_Tabiat_An%C4%B1t%C4%B1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abies_nordmanniana","wikidata":"Q148920"},{"title":"Nordmann","blocks":[{"text":"Nordmann is the demonym of the Norwegian people in its native language."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nordmann","wikidata":"Q120715"},{"title":"Fir","blocks":[{"text":"Firs are coniferous trees belonging to the genus Abies in the family Pinaceae. There are approximately 48–65 extant species, found on mountains throughout much of North and Central America, Eurasia, and North Africa. The genus is most closely related to Keteleeria, a small genus confined to eastern Asia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Abies_koreana_%28szyszki%29.JPG/330px-Abies_koreana_%28szyszki%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fir","wikidata":"Q25350"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Hortus